  speakerName: 
  storyText: '/* AUDIO: Ticking Clock Room Tone */'
  narrativeBeats:
  - /* Variable Defaults */
  - /* Setup Physical Bypass Costs */
  - UNIT 408 - THE KEYPAD
  - "Professor Harmon taught history and behavioral sociology at the university. You'd chatted with him in the elevator a few times \u2014 he always smelled like old paper and peppermint tea. He talked about the psychology of collapsing civilizations the way most people talked about the weather. Inevitable. Fascinating. Nothing personal."
  - The door is sealed with a heavy electronic lock. A small keypad glows faintly in the dark hallway, its LEDs casting a cold blue light across your fingers. Four blank digits. Waiting.
  - 'Someone has taped a yellowed index card above the scanner. The handwriting is spidery, hurried, and precise:'
  - '"If I''m not answering, I''m either dead or I finally took my own advice and ran.

    Either way, you''re not getting in."'
  - You almost smile. Almost.
  - "\u26D4 PERMANENTLY LOCKED OUT. The keypad triggered its security failsafe after three wrong attempts. The software is sealed. You will have to bypass it physically.\r\n                        \r\n                        \r\n                    \r\n                    \r\n                    \r\n                        \r\n                            \u2699\uFE0F HOW DO YOU PROCEED?"
  - 1 Minute | You saw a text from him earlier. You didn't know what it was for at the time. Now you do.
  - "0>>\r\n                                \r\n                                    \u26A0\uFE0F WRONG CODE. Attempts remaining: . Three failures trigger the lockout permanently."
  - "= 3>>\r\n                                            \r\n                                        \r\n                                        \r\n                                    \r\n                                \r\n                                1 Minute | Four digits. Think carefully \u2014 you only get three attempts before the failsafe triggers."
  - "\u26A0\uFE0F HARDWARE BYPASS"
  - "\u274C BRUTE FORCE FAILED. You battered the housing, but the internal deadbolt didn't budge. Your hands are bleeding, and you just wasted precious energy."
  - "[BURGLAR] Cost:  STAMINA. You've cracked tougher systems than this apartment lock.\r\n                                \r\n                            \r\n                                \r\n                                    Override the electronic latch\n\r\n                                    [REQUIRES BURGLAR] You lack the specialized knowledge to trick the mechanism."
  - "[LOCKSMITH] Cost:  STAMINA. Every electronic lock has a physical override pin. You find it.\r\n                                \r\n                            \r\n                                \r\n                                    Exploit the failsafe\n\r\n                                    [REQUIRES LOCKSMITH] You don't know where the physical override pin is located."
  - "= 2>>\r\n                                \r\n                                    \r\n                                        \r\n                                    \r\n                                    [TECH 2] Cost:  STAMINA. You pull the panel and bridge the latch relay wire.\r\n                                \r\n                            \r\n                                \r\n                                    Bypass the keypad circuit\n\r\n                                    [REQUIRES TECH 2] You lack the knowledge to safely hotwire the board."
  - "i.id === \"Multi-Tool\")>>\r\n                                \r\n                                    \r\n                                        \r\n                                    \r\n                                    [MULTI-TOOL] Cost:  STAMINA. You unscrew the faceplate and retract the deadbolt.\r\n                                \r\n                            \r\n                                \r\n                                    Disassemble the housing\n\r\n                                    [REQUIRES MULTI-TOOL] You don't have tools to take the faceplate off."
  - "= 6 and not $room408_locked_out>>\r\n                                \r\n                                    \r\n                                        \r\n                                    \r\n                                    [PER 6] Cost: 0 STAMINA. The 8, 4, and 5 keys have heavy smudges. You guess the sequence.\r\n                                \r\n                            \r\n                                \r\n                                    Read the finger smudges\n\r\n                                    [REQUIRES PER 6] Your eyes aren't sharp enough to pick up wear patterns."
  - "= 6>>\r\n                                \r\n                                    \r\n                                        \r\n                                    \r\n                                    \r\n                                        [STR /6] Cost:  STAMINA. Your high Strength guarantees you can shatter the housing easily without triggering the alarm.\r\n                                    \r\n                                \r\n                            \r\n                                \r\n                                    \r\n                                        \r\n                                    \r\n                                    \r\n                                        [STR /6] You aren't strong enough to just rip it off. You'll have to time your strikes perfectly to hit the weak point."
  - UNIT 408 - THE PROFESSOR'S STUDY
  - The heavy door swings open into darkness.
  - 'The smell reaches you first: old paper, dust, and something faintly sweet like peppermint. But there is also the stark emptiness of a room that has been hastily abandoned.'
  - The Professor is gone. Drawers are pulled open. His heavy winter coat and hiking backpack are missing from the coat rack. But he couldn't take the books. Floor-to-ceiling shelves line all four walls. Journals and monographs are stacked three deep on the coffee table.
  - "His reading glasses sit folded on an open book \u2014 The Fall of Rome, marked with a yellow sticky note:"
  - '"Every empire ends. We''re just living in the intermission. Take what you need."'
  - "\U0001F4DA WHAT DO YOU DO?"
  - "You don't have time to read entire books while the city burns outside. But Harmon didn't just leave books\u2014he left survival manuals with frantic, handwritten notes shoved between the pages."
  - "[TECH +1] You flip through the bookmarked pages. His notes on jury-rigging engines and bypassing civilian security systems are brilliant. You memorize what you can.\r\n                        \r\n                    \r\n                        \r\n                            \U0001F4D6 You've already stripped the engineering textbook of all its useful notes."
  - "[MEDICINE +1] He aggressively highlighted chapters on trauma care, blood-borne pathogens, and the central nervous system. You commit the diagrams to memory.\r\n                        \r\n                    \r\n                        \r\n                            \U0001F4D6 You've already absorbed the highlighted trauma care procedures."
  - "[PER +1] His handwriting degrades into a frantic scrawl toward the end. He documented unmarked FEMA transports operating at night and the CDC's blackout protocols.\r\n                        \r\n                    \r\n                        \r\n                            \U0001F4D3 You've already read the journal and added the intel to your PDA."
  - He packed light, leaving the heavier items behind. You find canned food, an energy bar, and sealed bottles of water.
  - You find a heavy, hard-bound Encyclopedia (could be used for blunt force) and a fully charged Flashlight.
  - "You've stripped the room of everything valuable \u2014 knowledge and supplies both. The rest is just dead weight."
  dialogueLines:
  - introNarration: 
    speakerName: You
    side: 0
    avatarSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 04a95c7136264fc6d4e69cfcfe253bf5, type: 3}
    animatedAvatarFrames: []
    avatarFPS: 8
    dialogueText: Dark sense of humor. I hope you made it out of the city, Professor.
    outroNarration: 
    requiresStoryFlag: 
    requiresNotFlag: 
  - introNarration: 
    speakerName: You
    side: 0
    avatarSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 04a95c7136264fc6d4e69cfcfe253bf5, type: 3}
    animatedAvatarFrames: []
    avatarFPS: 8
    dialogueText: Damn it. It bricked itself. Time to do this the hard way.
    outroNarration: 
    requiresStoryFlag: 
    requiresNotFlag: 
  - introNarration: 
    speakerName: You
    side: 0
    avatarSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 04a95c7136264fc6d4e69cfcfe253bf5, type: 3}
    animatedAvatarFrames: []
    avatarFPS: 8
    dialogueText: He didn't just see this coming. He packed up and left before the alarms even started.
    outroNarration: 
    requiresStoryFlag: 
    requiresNotFlag: 
